H0  CONSTANTS AND THRESHOLDS  (Theorem D: Phi_T(w) irrational whenever Dio(w) > eta(w) = mu(beta))
==============================================================================================================
  Bugeaud-Kim (TAMS 371 (2019)) Thm 3.4/3.6: rep(s) <= sqrt10 - 3/2 = 1.6622776602 for every (quasi-)Sturmian s;
    Lemma 10.3: Dio = rep/(rep-1)  ->  Dio(s) >= 2.5099407094  (= 5/3 + 4 sqrt10/15 = 2.5099407094)
  Theorem S (options A/B, limsup q_(n+1)/q_n >= phi): mu(mu-1) < phi  <=>  mu < 1.8667603992;  ADQZ/BHZ initial squares: mu < 2
