  Height exponent mu(beta) = max(1, beta log2 m1) for T(x) = x/2, (m1 x + 1)/2  (m0 = 1, r1 = 1):
    map    | log2 m1 | critical beta | beta range with mu < Dio_BK (all Sturmian & quasi-Sturmian) | mu < 2 (ADQZ) | mu < 1.8668 (Thm S)
    3x+1   |  1.5850 |        0.6309 | beta < 1.0000 (ALL slopes) | beta < 1.0000 | beta < 1.0000
    5x+1   |  2.3219 |        0.4307 | beta < 1.0000 (ALL slopes) | beta < 0.8614 | beta < 0.8040
    7x+1   |  2.8074 |        0.3562 | beta < 0.8941 | beta < 0.7124 | beta < 0.6650
    9x+1   |  3.1699 |        0.3155 | beta < 0.7918 | beta < 0.6309 | beta < 0.5889
    19x+1  |  4.2479 |        0.2354 | beta < 0.5909 | beta < 0.4708 | beta < 0.4395
    Mahler ceil(3a/2): m0 = m1 = 3, mu = log2 3 = 1.5850 < Dio_BK: every Sturmian/quasi-Sturmian carry word.
  Lemma P (2-adic Tschakaloff, Theorem Y): sum_(k>=0) rho^(k^2) is irrational in Q_2 for rho = 2^L/M (M odd) whenever mu_bar = max(1, log2(M)/L) < phi = 1.618034; with the unshifted construction (m = 0): mu_bar < 3/2.
  Linear complexity (AB ETDS 2007, proof of Thm 3): p(n) <= c n infinitely often => Dio >= 1 + 1/c; 3x+1 needs c < 1/(beta log2 3 - 1), e.g. beta = 0.9: c < 2.345; beta = 1: c < 1.710
