C1  SUPERCRITICAL STRIPS: automaton, entropy, E-sets K_q (E = -Phi_R of the tail), decoupled-Mahler pressure
==============================================================================================================
  strip(A/B, W): states k = B a_s - A s in [0, floor(BW)]; letter 1: k += B-A, letter 0: k -= A.
  K_q = {E(w') : w' strip tail from q}, E(1w) = 1/3 + 2E(w)/3, E(0w) = 2E(w).  If the one-step images of the hulls
  overlap at every state, K_q = [lo_q, hi_q] exactly (graph-directed IFS; 'overlap' column).  m_q = min(1, hi_q - lo_q)
  = measure of frac(K_q) then.  Decoupled pressure P_MZ = log2(3^alpha/2) + log2 rho(A_q,q' m_q'): P_MZ > 0 means the
  word-free Mahler relaxation MZ is heuristically FALSE (vacuous when all m_q = 1); P_MZ < 0 means MZ is non-vacuous
  and heuristically TRUE, and MZ => C2 for that strip (Proposition M).  Where 'overlap' is False, m_q is the hull
  length, an upper bound for the measure of frac(K_q), so the printed P_MZ is an upper bound.
  'forced cycle' = a cycle through states with a single allowed letter (Proposition Rnd needs: none).
   alpha  |  W  | states | entropy(bits/letter) | E hull            | overlap | min/max m_q   | #q with m_q<1 | P_MZ   | forced cycle
