      u=-    v=1            supercritical=True: P/Q = -1  real series = -1.0  |diff| = 2.67e-51
      u=-    v=110          supercritical=True: P/Q = -5  real series = -5.0  |diff| = 7.35e-46
      u=01   v=110          supercritical=True: P/Q = -22/3  real series = -7.333333333333333333333333  |diff| = 7.74e-46
      u=-    v=11101        supercritical=True: P/Q = -73/49  real series = -1.48979591836734693877551  |diff| = 3.74e-50
      u=100  v=1101110      supercritical=True: P/Q = -2411/345  real series = -6.988405797101449275362319  |diff| = 9.7e-48
      u=-    v=11110111001  supercritical=True: P/Q = -8113/4513  real series = -1.7976955461998670507423  |diff| = 2.92e-48
  (ii) tail recursion E_(s+1) = E_s/2 (w_s = 0), (3E_s - 1)/2 (w_s = 1), E_s = -Phi_R(sigma^s w) > 0, on a 3/4-strip word:
      E_0..E_7 = ['3.7341614', '1.8670807', '2.3006211', '2.9509316', '1.4754658', '1.7131987', '2.069798', '2.6046971']; recursion holds to 1e-20: True
  [215s]
==============================================================================================================
C4  WHY THE PROVED MECHANISMS STOP (measurements)
==============================================================================================================
   alpha  | lambda = 3^alpha/2 | orbit values <= X (hypothetical strip orbit) | Monks-Yazinski liminf a_s/s >= log_3 2 = 0.6309
    0.65  |             1.0212 | ~ log X / log lambda =  47.73 log X (density zero)  | satisfied (0.65 > 0.6309)
    0.70  |             1.0788 | ~ log X / log lambda =  13.18 log X (density zero)  | satisfied (0.70 > 0.6309)
    0.75  |             1.1398 | ~ log X / log lambda =   7.64 log X (density zero)  | satisfied (0.75 > 0.6309)
    0.80  |             1.2041 | ~ log X / log lambda =   5.38 log X (density zero)  | satisfied (0.80 > 0.6309)
    0.90  |             1.3439 | ~ log X / log lambda =   3.38 log X (density zero)  | satisfied (0.90 > 0.6309)
    0.95  |             1.4198 | ~ log X / log lambda =   2.85 log X (density zero)  | satisfied (0.95 > 0.6309)
   capacity (in-house (D2)-(D2c)) needs n_j <= C j; supercritical strips give n_j >= c lambda^j: the counting inequality
   N <= #{admissible integers <= C lambda^N} ~ lambda^N / 3 always holds, and E_eps (density zero) contains the orbit
   without contradiction.  [215s]
DONE [215s]
